id: pm-slack-standup-murn
title: Show declared decision requests in periodic standups
description: "Present explicit human or agent decision requests with alternatives, response deadlines, canonical evidence and acknowledgment links."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: added,decisions,standup
created_at: "2026-10-21T20:31:22.856Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-22T15:45:40.706Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Only declared requests appear; closed and superseded decisions disappear deterministically; private alternatives respect disclosure policy. Typed SDK and CLI provide bounded TOON/JSON with typed refusals and remedies; README and example; non-git public tracker validation; npm and Bun CI release gates.
comments[21]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T20:31:41.362Z",codex-agent,"Overlap rechecked against CLI 2026.10.21 and pinned SDK 2026.10.17: core plan decision stores text, rationale and evidence; pm-brief decisionsNeeded selects active Decision items for general context; pm-slack owns notification transport. No existing explicit decision-request standup contract was found. This feature owns periodic presentation and acknowledgment linkage only. Reconciliation PR #141 items are excluded. Plan: an explicit standup-decision-request tag plus a versioned declaration in the item body; public-only alternative disclosure, terminal/superseded suppression, deterministic bounded SDK and CLI reports, opt-in standup section, non-git regressions and public tracker copy validation. Dependency pins stay unchanged."
  "2026-10-21T20:37:56.113Z",codex-agent,"Implemented public typed declaration/report/refusal contracts, read-only standup decisions command, and opt-in periodic sections. Limits: at most 10 rows, default compact JSON projection budget 8192 bytes, whole-row omissions with counts and remedy. Tagged requests are excluded from ordinary work buckets when enabled so JSON exports cannot copy private alternatives from source bodies. Deadlines and IDs define ordering; terminal states suppress obsolete declarations. Local targeted checks and real no-git lifecycle tests are being verified; CI runs both npm and Bun full release gates without lowering thresholds."
  "2026-10-21T20:39:54.308Z",codex-agent,"Read-only public snapshot validation at main 765b440ce656692c73bbcbafb5102ac3b3c8324b: 96 complete items (5 in_progress, 5 open, 84 closed, 2 canceled), 2 Decision items, 0 explicitly declared requests, 0 emitted/omitted. Compact JSON report 201 bytes; full plain standup 8172 bytes. All 198 copied tracker files remained SHA-256 identical. Copy had no git directory; source files were read-only. Positive SDK/registered CLI tests use a separate initialized non-git tracker and a PATH with Node and pm only. Targeted new-module c8 evidence: 100% statements/branches/functions/lines, 5/5 tests."
  "2026-10-21T20:40:30.227Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: replaced only collectDecisionRequests with the pre-feature empty-section behavior, rebuilt dist, and ran node --test --test-name-pattern=\"only declared|periodic text\" test/decision-requests.test.ts. Both selected regressions failed (0 pass, 2 fail), including missing active requests and missing periodic presentation. Restored the implementation and rebuilt. Adjacent exporter/unit regressions pass 93/93; typecheck, test typecheck, lint, docstring (102 declarations) and duplication (0%) pass. No full local release gate was run because of the CPU constraint."
  "2026-10-21T20:42:52.200Z",codex-agent,"Pinned pm test runner passed the linked decision regressions: 5 tests, 5 pass, 0 failures. Result tracking is disabled by existing project policy, so the receipt is recorded here without changing that policy. Local health has an existing global-extension host/SDK version-skew finding; tracker history and item data were not repaired or rewritten. Full CI uses clean installed dependencies. CLI and SDK pins remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-21T20:49:06.736Z",codex-agent,"CI run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack-standup/actions/runs/39672895443 caught a missing preflight scope registration for standup decisions: Node 26 had 269 pass, 1 fail, and 100% statements/branches/functions/lines across all 12 authored source files. Added the command to the scope and command-list contract; local smoke tests now pass 6/6. Strengthened privacy so declared request bodies never enter ordinary export buckets, even with the optional section off. Removing only that filtering from buildStandupData and rebuilding made the privacy regression fail (0 pass, 1 fail); restored and green. Latest decision tests pass 5/5. A second public-copy read with Node only on PATH and a Git discovery ceiling confirms 96 items and 0 declared requests."
  "2026-10-21T20:49:07.728Z",codex-agent,"Ready PR #142 contains the full implementation and measured validation: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack-standup/pull/142 . Exact final-head npm and Bun release gate run URLs and pass counts will be reported in the PR after CI completes. Automated review is unavailable: Sourcery quota exhausted, Greptile trial ended, CodeRabbit skipped automatic review. These are missing review evidence, not approvals. No merge or release is authorized; leave the feature in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-22T09:36:30.535Z",pi-agent,"Review round for PR 142: four unresolved threads are valid. Refusal messages will name the canonical item id (CLI prints only the message). Terminal matching will include the standup done alias complete and trim status before comparing, so padded closed items are suppressed before payload validation. Block Kit decision sections will chunk on line boundaries under the 2400 UTF-16 bound so evidence and acknowledgment URLs are not split. A multi-byte outputBytes regression will fail if the budget uses UTF-16 length instead of UTF-8 bytes. Latest CodeRabbit review body had four inline comments and no Outside diff range findings."
  "2026-10-22T09:42:08.820Z",pi-agent,"Revert proofs, each restored before the next. Constructor message reverted to omit the item id: the invalid-declaration test failed because the message lacked the item. Terminal set without complete and status compared without trim: the lifecycle test threw invalid_request instead of suppressing padded complete and closed items. Block Kit chunking reverted to a 1200-code-point cut: the periodic test failed because a 1548-unit evidence line was not intact in any block. Budget comparison reverted from byte length to string length: the emoji budget test failed because UTF-8 size exceeded 1024 while UTF-16 length did not. Docstring, lint and duplication gates passed on the restored fix."
  "2026-10-22T10:08:41.831Z",codex-agent,"Continuation review for PR #142: fetched every unresolved thread and all comments; four threads, no pagination gaps, and no outside-diff findings in the latest CodeRabbit review. Remote branch is current and already contains main. Reviewed the inherited draft and whole feature diff; retained the four valid fixes, strengthened the actual CLI refusal assertion, and will independently repeat all behavioral revert proofs before npm and Bun release gates. Previous claim transferred because that provider session ended."
  "2026-10-22T10:13:34.409Z",codex-agent,"Independent continuation proofs: node --test test/decision-requests.test.ts passed 5/5 including real CLI refusal item identity and non-git SDK lifecycle. Five isolated behavioral mutants each failed exactly one selected test with exit 1: constructor message without item id (invalid options pattern), missing complete alias (only declared), missing status trim (only declared), original fixed-offset Block Kit chunking (periodic text), and JSON string length instead of UTF-8 byte length (deadline and ID). Each source was restored byte-identically in a finally block; no reverted-for-proof implementation remains. Thread mappings: PRRT_kwDOTbNzVM6u_hTU refusal identity; PRRT_kwDOTbNzVM6u_hTe terminal alias plus normalization; PRRT_kwDOTbNzVM6u_hTj intact link lines; PRRT_kwDOTbNzVM6u_hTs multibyte budget regression. Whole PR inspected for the same defect classes; no additional instances found."
  "2026-10-22T10:37:26.687Z",codex-agent,"Validation before CI: npm ci passed with zero vulnerabilities; pinned linked pure regressions passed 4/4. Strict clean-identity pm health passed after preserving the pinned installer-generated extension merge fence; no history repair or gate change. Full local clean-identity npm run release:check reached 270 tests: 267 passed, 3 failed, zero skipped/canceled/todo. Two existing packed-matrix test subprocesses hit ETIMEDOUT at their fixed five-minute limits; the HTTPS fallback test observed ECONNRESET instead of HTTP 503. Isolated clean-identity node --test --test-name-pattern=\"real HTTPS failures\" test/runtime-transport.test.ts passed 1/1 on retry. The decision module measured 100% in all four dimensions; whole-source coverage was incomplete because of those existing failing paths, so the local release gate is not claimed as passed. Exact pushed-head CI must pass both full npm and Bun release gates at unchanged thresholds before acceptance. No new pm CLI/SDK API defect observed; automatic result persistence remains disabled by existing policy."
  "2026-10-22T10:58:32.861Z",codex-agent,"Exact code-head CI acceptance at 081849f25453a5f1471ef52ce9f097cd57256e1e: run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack-standup/actions/runs/39764651988 Node 26 job 119776988596 passed both npm run release:check and bun run release:check. Each ran 270/270 tests, zero failures/skips/canceled/todo, and measured all 12 runtime source files at 100 percent statements/branches/functions/lines. Each also passed canonical-reader acceptance 1/1 and all 5 packed npm/Bun host scenarios, zero production vulnerabilities, zero duplication, 102 documented declarations, changelog and publication gates. Thus the two local packed timeouts pass in CI; the local HTTPS reset passed both isolated retry 1/1 and CI. Stopped the redundant local Bun gate after CI passed; it is not counted as a local pass. Windows CI passed 22 launcher tests, 13 platform-specific skips, zero failures, plus all 5 packed scenarios. Node 22 is still finishing at this receipt. This final receipt changes tracker data only; final pushed-head checks will also be verified before PR #141. Existing health advisories remain, with no new pm CLI/SDK API defect observed. Leave in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-22T13:10:48.823Z",codex-agent,"Review round 2: worktree and upstream are clean/current at f55f15d; main is already contained. Re-read all unresolved threads and comments plus latest CodeRabbit body: one new valid thread PRRT_kwDOTbNzVM6vMWp8, no outside-diff findings or pagination gaps. Two enum guards in declaration coerce untrusted JSON with String, accepting singleton arrays or throwing untyped TypeError for objects with a null toString property. Replace both with original-value comparisons and add separate audience/disclosure regressions covering arrays, objects, null, booleans and numbers. Self-review found no other declaration enum coercion; state, top-level disclosure, labels and links already validate original values. Existing PR #141 work and prior verified fixes are retained."
  "2026-10-22T13:12:33.700Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 regression proof for PRRT_kwDOTbNzVM6vMWp8: the two new non-string enum tests first failed 0/2 on the pre-fix code, accepting singleton arrays instead of refusing. After direct original-value comparisons, the complete decision suite passed 7/7, including real non-git SDK/CLI lifecycle tests. Independently restored only the audience coercion guard: selected audience regression failed 0/1 with Missing expected exception. Restored the fix, then restored only the alternative disclosure coercion guard: its selected regression failed 0/1. Fixed source restored byte-identically in finally blocks; targeted restored tests pass 2/2 and the pinned linked runner passes 2/2. Arrays, nested arrays, objects with null or non-callable toString, undefined/null, booleans and numbers all produce item-scoped invalid_request, exit 2, without secret labels in the error. Whole-PR same-class review confirmed other declaration fields validate original values and contain no further enum coercion. Rebuilt committed dist and updated the packaged schema documentation; pins and thresholds unchanged."
  "2026-10-22T13:33:58.407Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 local gates: clean-identity npm run release:check passed 272/272, zero failures/skips/canceled/todo, all 12 runtime sources at 100 percent statements/branches/functions/lines, canonical-reader 1/1, all 5 packed scenarios, and every remaining release check. The first Bun full gate passed 271/272; only the existing inherited-npm_execpath packed matrix reached its unchanged 290-second subprocess deadline (ETIMEDOUT). All source coverage dimensions were 100 percent and both new enum tests passed. This same matrix passed in the npm gate. Retry only the failed full Bun gate with the existing package cache and clean Git identity; no assertion, timeout, dependency or threshold change."
  "2026-10-22T13:42:03.310Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 acceptance complete: clean-identity npm run release:check and bun run release:check both passed locally on Node 26.12.0, each 272/272 tests with zero failures/skips/canceled/todo, all 12 runtime sources at 100 percent statements/branches/functions/lines, canonical-reader 1/1, and all 5 packed npm/Bun current/minimum/global scenarios. Both gates passed typecheck, lint, build, zero duplication (0/9805 lines), 102 documented declarations, zero production vulnerabilities, package/changelog/date/attestation checks. The first Bun attempt had one inherited-npm_execpath ETIMEDOUT at its existing 290-second limit; the full retry passed with the existing package cache. No assertions, timeouts, thresholds or dependencies changed. Two independent revert proofs and 7/7 focused plus 2/2 linked results are recorded above. Committed dist is rebuilt. No new pm CLI/SDK API defect observed; existing project policy disables linked-test result persistence. Leave in progress and release ownership for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-22T15:15:05.001Z",codex-agent,"Review round 3: upstream and worktree clean at 1759c44; main is contained. Read all comments in every unresolved thread and latest CodeRabbit body with no pagination gaps or outside-diff findings. Two valid findings: PRRT_kwDOTbNzVM6vQFWf documents build:test although it emits no dist, and PRRT_kwDOTbNzVM6vQFWv reads the tracker before validating decision bounds. Add the production build to the documented standalone sequence; validate parsed options through collectDecisionRequests before the canonical read, retaining one source of bounds rules. Add real non-git failing-reader regression and demonstrate documented build necessity in an isolated source copy. Preserve earlier reviewed fixes and PR #141."
  "2026-10-22T15:20:38.861Z",codex-agent,"Round 3 regression proofs: removing only the handler precheck makes the retained option regression fail 0/1 because an actual strict canonical read of a corrupted item overrides invalid_options. Fixed handler restores all eight invalid string-bound cases to typed invalid_options, exit 2, no item ID; valid bounds still surface the source failure. Removing only npm run build from the validation guide makes its integration regression fail 0/1 with TS2307: build:test imports dist through the public consumer fixture. The build must precede build:test as well as standalone execution. Both fixed files restored byte-identically in finally blocks. Focused node --test test/decision-requests.test.ts test/decision-validation-guide.test.ts passes 9/9, no failures/skips/canceled/todo; linked selected regressions pass 2/2. The guide regression copies actual source/configuration into a fresh non-git directory without dist, executes every documented command and requires nonempty successful child-test receipts with inherited runner context removed. Whole-PR review found no other instance: package test/coverage scripts already build first, CI checks committed dist, standup/export resolve presentation options before source reads, and the SDK example supplies fixed valid bounds. npm ci passed 165 packages added, 206 audited, zero vulnerabilities. Full npm and Bun release gates follow at unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-22T15:32:09.885Z",codex-agent,"Round 3 local npm release gate: 272/274 passed, zero skips/canceled/todo. Only the two existing packed acceptance matrices (npm_execpath inherited and unset) failed, each ETIMEDOUT at its unchanged 290-second subprocess bound. Both new regressions passed, including the documentation recipe executing actual child tests. Whole-source coverage is incomplete (98.2 statements/lines, 99.83 branches, 99.29 functions) because packed acceptance paths timed out; the decision module itself is 100 percent in all four dimensions. Do not claim local full release acceptance. Full Bun gate is being attempted separately. Push the code, rebuilt dist and these honest receipts for CI verification of both complete release gates at the exact code head, with all 100 percent thresholds, assertions and timeouts retained."
  "2026-10-22T15:45:39.597Z",codex-agent,"Round 3 acceptance verified at exact code head c69a38ba35ea8368b60246727f39e696e9f7ea49: CI run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-slack-standup/actions/runs/39805987166 succeeded. Node 26 job 119919205775 and Node 22.18.0 job 119919206134 each passed BOTH npm run release:check and bun run release:check: 274/274 per gate, zero failures/skips/canceled/todo, all 12 runtime sources at 100 percent statements/branches/functions/lines, canonical-reader 1/1 and all 5 packed npm/Bun current/minimum/global scenarios. Each gate passed zero duplication (0/9857 lines), 102 documented declarations, production audit, package/changelog/date/attestation checks. CI also verified strict PM health and rebuilt committed dist. Local npm was 272/274 with two existing packed-matrix ETIMEDOUTs; local Bun was 271/274 with those two timeouts plus the existing HTTPS hang case seeing ECONNRESET instead of its timeout message. The HTTPS case passed isolated clean-identity retry 1/1; all local failing cases passed both full gates on both CI Node versions. Thus the host timeouts have passing CI evidence; no thresholds, assertions or existing timeouts were weakened. Revert proofs 0/1 each, restored focused 9/9 and linked 2/2 are recorded above. This final receipt changes tracker metadata only. No new pm CLI/SDK API defect observed; linked-test persistence remains disabled by project policy. Leave in progress and release ownership for orchestrator verification."
